.TH btctax-reconcile-link-transfer 1  btctax "btctax manual"
.SH NAME
link\-transfer \- Confirm a self\-transfer (TransferLink)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlink\-transfer\fR [\fB\-\-to\-event\fR] [\fB\-\-to\-wallet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIOUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Confirm a self\-transfer (TransferLink)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-to\-event\fR \fI<TO_EVENT>\fR
The destination `TransferIn` event this outflow arrived as. PREFER THIS whenever the arrival is in the ledger: it consumes that deposit, so the coins are relocated exactly once
.TP
\fB\-\-to\-wallet\fR \fI<TO_WALLET>\fR
The destination WALLET, when its arrival was never imported. This form names no in\-event, so it cannot consume one: if a deposit at this wallet turns out to be the other leg, btctax raises a hard "self\-transfer double\-booking" blocker naming both — booking both legs would relocate the coins AND mint a fresh lot for them, doubling the basis. Resolve it with `\-\-to\-event` or `reconcile match\-self\-transfers`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIOUT\fR>

